<task id="013" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-12 (A-18): Workforce contact-by-email resolution must apply the CIAM no-hijack oid check</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <gate>after-001</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <status-note>**RE-OPENED 2026-09-30** (owner Q7 approval, session 27). The no-hijack guard shipped here is INERT, because nothing in src writes a contact oid binding, so no contact is ever "bound to a different oid". That is defect C7. The notes at the time already said "Do not mark A-18 closed" (notes/wave2-parallel-merge-plan.md). The completing work is task 141, which builds the owner-approved identity binding (Entra oid stored in contact.sprk_externalobjectid, completing SPA-r2 FR-11 / task 023). See the amendments block. The history below is kept as written.

**Status corrected 2026-09-03 by a full project status audit.** The POML still read
`pending` while `TASK-INDEX.md` marked it ✅ and git carried completion evidence — the task was DONE and
only step 1 of root CLAUDE.md §7 ("update the task .poml status") had been skipped. This happened to **14
tasks**, systematically, because the index is updated during execution while the POML status is a separate
write that nothing enforces.

Evidence for THIS task: 41fbe7081 (Wave A tasks 011/013/015/018/020/081 merged and verified)

Two independent signals were required before flipping (git completion evidence AND the index marker); no
status was changed on the index alone.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on an identity-binding authorization path — an account-takeover vector under the multitenant workforce model (High) — FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8; security-sensitive per §6.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The correct guard already exists on the CIAM path and must be mirrored onto the workforce path; A-18 gives the exact source and target lines. Well-specified, but security-sensitive.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs — a known-contended directory (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**). Merge serially with /conflict-check.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001, 141</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close finding A-18 (spec FR-12, High): the workforce contact-by-email fallback binds a caller to a contact by raw emailaddress1 match with NO check of whether that contact is already bound to a DIFFERENT oid — the CIAM path already enforces this no-hijack guard, the workforce path does not. Under the multitenant workforce model a token's email claim is not domain-verified across a foreign tenant, so a caller carrying email=victim@firm.com inherits the victim's contact and grants. Apply the same oid no-hijack check on the workforce path: an email matching a contact bound to a different oid is denied.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Entra/CIAM identity claims, contact↔oid binding, and the Spaarke identity-normalization path. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The workforce contact-by-email resolution denies (does not resolve) when the matched contact is already bound to a different oid, mirroring the CIAM guard. A caller whose email matches a contact bound to another person's oid gets no principal and no grants.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-18 (10-finding-confirmations.md, ranked #4 High): workforce contact-only branch WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs:148-160 calls _identity.TryResolveContactByWorkforceIdentityAsync(callerOid, verifiedEmail, ct). That method (IdentityNormalizationService.cs:242-281) tries oid cross-ref first (:252-262) then falls back to a raw emailaddress1 match (:268-278 → TryResolveContactIdByEmailAsync:331-372) that returns the contact id with NO check of whether the contact is already bound to a DIFFERENT oid, and no oid-binding write. Contrast the CIAM path ExternalParticipationService.ResolveExternalContactAsync:211-258 which DENIES an email match on a contact already bound to a different oid (:247-257, "no email hijack of a bound Contact"). The trust hinge is cross-tenant verifiability of the email claim (WorkforcePrincipalResolver.ExtractVerifiedEmail:178-186). FR-12 acceptance: an email matching a contact bound to a different oid is denied.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/IdentityNormalizationService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/WorkforceEmailNoHijackTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="completed">Characterization test pinning the unguarded email fallback, flipped here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The no-hijack rule mirrors the CIAM path exactly (ExternalParticipationService.ResolveExternalContactAsync:247-257): a raw email match on a contact bound to a DIFFERENT oid is denied. Scope: the workforce contact-by-email fallback.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: ambiguity (multiple contacts match the email, or binding state cannot be read) DENIES — it does not pick one contact. Scope: the resolution path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT auto-write an oid binding as a side effect of a denied match; only an oid-verified resolution may create/confirm a binding. Scope: any binding write in the changed path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Both edited files are consumed by the BFF (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs ~44.96 MB baseline in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-001">OWN-COVERAGE OBLIGATION (owner decision 2026-08-21, path B). A-18: Extract the contact-by-email resolution decision from IdentityNormalizationService:242-281 so the no-hijack oid check is assertable without Dataverse. Task 001 could not pin A-18; this task owns that coverage. Tests go at tests/integration/auth/** (the ADR-038 KEEP path backfilled by task 001), following the Characterization_ + 'FLIPPED BY' convention there. Extract ONLY -- do not change behaviour in the same commit as the fix, so the pre-fix state can be pinned first. Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; stays banned (ADR-038 B1); if unavoidable, escalate as CLAUDE.md 6.5 path A rather than silently excepting. Scope: this task's test deliverable.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>identity binding no-hijack</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="spaarke-sso-binding" location=".claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md">Canonical v2 identity binding</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the CIAM guard (ExternalParticipationService.ResolveExternalContactAsync:211-258) and the unguarded workforce fallback (IdentityNormalizationService.cs:242-281, :331-372).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the no-hijack check to the workforce email fallback: when a contact matches by email, verify it is not bound to a different oid; if it is, return no-resolution (deny). Prefer centralizing the check so both call-sites share one implementation.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs:148-160 treats a denied resolution as no principal (fail-closed), not a partial principal.</step>
    <step order="4">Author WorkforceEmailNoHijackTests + flip the task-001 characterization test: email matching a contact bound to a different oid → denied; email matching an unbound contact or the caller's own bound contact → resolves.</step>
    <step order="5">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the shared no-hijack helper (if introduced) in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If legitimate workforce onboarding RELIES on the unguarded email fallback to first-bind a contact (no prior oid), STOP and escalate: distinguishing "unbound contact, safe to bind" from "bound to another oid, deny" is the crux — get the binding-state semantics confirmed before shipping.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests — existing BFF test project; no test covers the workforce contact-by-email no-hijack guard (the CIAM path has the guard; the workforce path was found unguarded by A-18).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a new test file inside the existing project; test surface for existing code, not new production surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the test, the account-takeover path (email matching a contact bound to a different oid) can regress silently under the multitenant workforce model (FR-12).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/IdentityNormalizationService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/WorkforceEmailNoHijackTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An email matching a contact bound to a DIFFERENT oid is denied on the workforce path (FR-12 acceptance) — no principal resolved, no grants inherited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An email matching an unbound contact, or the caller's own oid-bound contact, still resolves (no over-denial of legitimate callers).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: multiple contacts matching the email, or unreadable binding state, DENIES rather than picking one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a denied match does not write an oid binding as a side effect.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The workforce and CIAM paths apply the same no-hijack rule (code review confirms shared logic or exact mirror).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-12; finding A-18 (register §A.2 rank 4). Related prerequisite E-6 (multitenant app registration) is environment work, out of Phase 0 code scope — this task hardens the code path that E-6 makes reachable.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="session 26 defect verification (C7) and owner round-2 decision item 4 / Q3 / Q7 in session 27 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md; notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md)">
    <verdict>RE-OPENED. FR-12's acceptance ("an email matching a contact bound to a different oid is
    denied") passes in unit tests but never happens in production, because no contact is ever bound. The
    guard has nothing to guard. The completing work is task 141. No further code is authored under this id.</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" defect="C7" completing-task="141">
    Why the guard is inert, verified against current code:
    (a) ExtractVerifiedEmail (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs:220-226)
    verifies nothing. It returns email, else preferred_username, else upn.
    (b) The workforce contact branch (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/IdentityNormalizationService.cs:242,
    TryResolveContactByWorkforceIdentityAsync) binds on contact.azureactivedirectoryobjectid. Its own doc
    comment says "Nothing here writes a binding" (:478), and the only write of that column anywhere in src
    is to a SYSTEMUSER row (Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs:372).
    (c) In dev (spaarkedev1) contact has no azureactivedirectoryobjectid attribute at all. The email query
    selects it (:598), throws, and is caught as null. So every non-systemuser workforce caller is denied
    (403 principal_not_resolved), and the GuardInertNoBindingColumn warning (:353, emitted at :615-634)
    cannot fire. That is an availability defect for Type-2 employees.
    (d) Where the column exists but is empty, the unverified email claim is the only link, which is a
    hijack path.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2" title="Owner decision that task 141 implements (round 2 item 4, Q3 approved)">
    Link by Entra oid, stored in contact.sprk_externalobjectid, the column the CIAM invite already binds
    (the invite writes it at Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs:141-145; the CIAM first-login bind is ExternalParticipationService.BindOidToContactAsync, ~:460-493). A first-sign-in email bind
    happens ONLY for tenant members (not guests) with EXACTLY one matching contact. After that, the oid is
    the only link. Otherwise a contact keyed by oid is created. A collision (email matches a contact bound
    to another oid) is refused and flagged. This supersedes this task's "Do NOT auto-write an oid binding"
    constraint for the approved first-sign-in bind only. The constraint still holds for any DENIED match.
    Task 141 also removes the dependency on the absent contact.azureactivedirectoryobjectid column.</amendment>
    <acceptance-criteria-amended>
      <criterion testable="true">Task 141 is completed: a Type-2 employee (tenant member, no systemuser) with exactly one matching contact resolves on first sign-in, and that contact's sprk_externalobjectid then holds the caller's oid.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative: a second identity whose email matches that now-bound contact is refused (no principal, no grants), and the collision is flagged.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative: a guest (non-member) token, or an email matching two or more contacts, never binds.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Oid only after binding: once a contact is bound, a later sign-in by the same oid resolves to it even when the email claim has changed, and the email claim is not consulted. Asserted by test.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">No contact query names contact.azureactivedirectoryobjectid (task 141's source guard test is green), so the dev path no longer throws and is no longer caught as null.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev): an existing unlicensed home-tenant MEMBER test identity with no systemuser resolves after first sign-in and no longer gets 403 principal_not_resolved, and one of the live collision identities recorded by task 141 is refused and flagged. Recorded in notes (task 141 carries the escalation if no such member test account exists).</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Only then are this task's status and its TASK-INDEX marker set back to completed, and scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 is clean for id 013.</criterion>
    </acceptance-criteria-amended>
    <a18-closure date="2026-10-01" closed-by="task 141 (branch task/uac-r2-141)">
    The A-18 closure is task 141. The "do not mark A-18 closed" residual comment was removed from
    IIdentityNormalizationService.cs, and the inert GuardInertNoBindingColumn and the email-by-contact.azureactivedirectoryobjectid
    path it guarded were deleted. Every workforce, systemuser, CIAM and invite binding now runs one pure decision
    (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactBindingDecision.cs). The amended criteria map to task 141 evidence as follows:
    (1) first-sign-in bind: WorkforceEmailNoHijackTests.FirstSignIn_OfAMember_BindsTheOneUnboundMatch_InDFormat_PlaneWorkforce;
    (2) second identity refused and flagged: AnEmailMatchBoundToAnotherOid_Denies_FlagsOnce_AndWritesNothingElse;
    (3) guest or ambiguous never binds: ANonMember_GetsNoEmailBind_AndNoCreation_AndAnOwnDenyCode and TwoActiveContactsCarryingTheEmail_Deny_AndBothAreFlagged;
    (4) oid only after binding: TheNextSignIn_ResolvesByOid_EvenWhenTheEmailClaimDiffers;
    (5) no contact query names azureactivedirectoryobjectid: ContactAadObjectIdColumnGuardTests (shown to bite by seeding one);
    (6) the MANUAL LIVE GATE is PENDING (task 141 notes §8, gates G-1 to G-5, live identity test.user@demo.spaarke.com per owner T2).
    So criterion 7 holds this task at pending: its status and TASK-INDEX marker go back to completed only after
    task 141's live gate passes. The main session owns that status change.
    </a18-closure>
  </amendments>
</task>
